\v 14 Make¦2477 yourself¦2478 a wooden¦2480 chest\f + \fr 6:14 \ft The reader might have expected the word ‘ark’ here, but sadly the Latin word ‘arca’ meaning ‘large box, chest’ led to the English word ‘ark’ being invented, and why we can't use it here, is that now for most English readers, they picture a large boat in their minds when they hear that word. If you think about the ‘ark of the covenant’ that uses the same word, hopefully you can understand how anything like a ‘boat’ is the wrong word picture, hence we've gone back to translating the actual Hebrew word here.\f* out of¦2480 cypress. Build¦2484 rooms inside it, and¦2488 seal it¦2489 both inside¦2490 and¦2491 outside¦2491 with¦2492 resin.
\v 15 These are¦2495 the dimensions for it¦2497: 140m long¦2501, 23m wide¦2505, and¦2506 14m high¦2508.
