\v 8 \add ≈So¦8210\add* \add King\add* Abimelech¦8211 got up early¦8210 in¦8212 the morning¦8212 and¦8213 called¦8213 for all¦8214 of¦8216 his¦8216 slaves \add to come\add*, and¦8217 he¦8217 explained the entire situation to them and¦8225 they¦8225 were¦8225 very¦8227 scared¦8225.
\v 9 Then¦8229 \add *he¦8230\add* sent for Abraham¦8231 and¦8232 asked¦8232 him¦8233, “What¦8234 have¦8236 you¦8236 done¦8236 to¦8237 us? What¦8238 did I¦8240 do to¦8241 you¦8241 that¦8252 you¦8244 would¦8255 cause all this trouble for me¦8245 and¦8246 my¦8248 people? What you¦8256 did¦8256 to me¦8257 should never have happened.”
\v 10 Then¦8259 \add *he¦8260\add* asked¦8259 \add again\add*, “What¦8264 were you¦8265 thinking when¦8266 you¦8267 did¦8267 that¦8271?”
\p
\v 11 “Because¦8275 I¦8276 thought that¦8283 there's¦8278 probably no one around here who \add obeys\add* God¦8281,” replied Abraham¦8274 “so¦8284 they¦8284 might kill¦8284 me¦8284 because of¦8287 my¦8288 wife¦8288.
\v 12 \add Besides that,\add* \add @Sarah\add* actually \em is¦8293\em* my¦8293 \add half-\add*sister¦8293. We have the¦8294 same father¦8296, but different \add #mothers¦8302\add*, and¦8303 then it¦8303 was her that I took as a¦8306 wife¦8306.
\v 13 \add Later\add* when¦8308 God¦8312 got me to leave my¦8314 father's¦8314 home¦8325, I¦8315 said¦8315 to¦8316 her¦8316, ‘You could do this¦8317 one kindness¦8318 do¦8320 for me¦8321: Everywhere¦8323 we¦8327 go¦8327, just¦8309 tell¦8329 them that¦8319 he's your brother¦8332.’ ”
