\v 5 because Abraham¦11473 obeyed¦11472 me by keeping¦11475 my¦11474 requirements, my¦11476 commands¦11477, my decrees, and¦11479 my¦11479 laws¦11479.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦11481\add* Yitshak¦11482 settled \add there\add* in¦11483 Gerar¦11483.
\v 7 Then¦11485 the¦11486 men¦11486 of¦11486 the¦11487 place¦11487 asked¦11485 about¦11488 his¦11488 wife, and¦11489 he¦11489 said¦11489, “She's my¦11490 sister¦11490,” because¦11492 he¦11493 was¦11493 afraid¦11493 to¦11494 say¦11494, “She's my wife.” He was thinking, “What if the¦11499 men¦11499 in this place¦11500 kill¦11498 me¦11498 because Rebekah¦11503 is¦11506 so beautiful to look at.”\x + \xo 26:7: \xt Gen 12:13; 20:2.\x*
\v 8 Then when he'd¦11510 been¦11510 in that area for¦11511 quite a while, the¦11516 Philistine King¦11519 Abimelech¦11518 looked¦11517 down¦11517 from a window¦11522 and¦11523 saw¦11523 that \add to his surprise\add*, Yitshak¦11525 was¦11526 laughing \add together\add* with¦11527 his¦11529 wife¦11529 Rebekah¦11528.
