\v 7 \add In due course\add* Yacob's¦16316 sons¦16315 came¦16317 \add home\add* from¦16318 the¦16320 countryside¦16320. When they¦16321 heard¦16321 \add what had happened\add*, then¦16322 they¦16322 \add ≈were¦16322 very¦16326 angry¦16322\add* \add and upset\add*, because¦16327 \add @Shekem¦16330\add* had¦16330 done¦16330 something disgraceful¦16329 to Yisra'el¦16331 by¦16332 \add ≈taking advantage of¦16335\add* Yacob's¦16337 daughter¦16335. \add Something like that should never have happened\add*.
