\v 9 \add In fact,\add* \add ^why don't\add* \add you allow us to marry\add* your¦16359 daughters, and you \add people could have\add* our¦16365 daughters \add ≡to marry\add*,
\v 10 then¦16369 you could settle \add here permanently\add* with¦16369 us¦16369. \add This region would open up to you all so\add* settle in it and trade \add with us\add* and \add you could\add* buy \add more land around here\add*.”
\p
\v 11 Then¦16379 Shekem¦16380 spoke¦16379 to¦16381 \add @Dinah's\add* father¦16383 and¦16385 brothers¦16387, “\add Look kindly on my request\add* and¦16392 I'll¦16395 give¦16395 \add whatever you ask for\add*.
