\p
\v 13 ⇔\add But because\add* \add @Shekem\add* had¦16428 \add abused\add* their¦16431 sister¦16431 Dinah¦16430, Yacob's¦16417 sons¦16415 \add gave a false answer\add* to Shekem¦16420 and¦16421 his¦16424 father¦16424,
\v 14 \add stating\add*, “\add Sorry,\add* we¦16436 can't¦16435 do¦16437 that¦16439 because¦16449 it would be¦16451 a¦16451 disgrace¦16451 \add in our culture\add* to allow a¦16444 man¦16444 with a¦16448 foreskin¦16448 \add to marry her\add*.
\v 15 We'd only¦16455 consent \add to your proposal\add* if¦16460 you'd¦16461 become like¦16462 us¦16462 by¦16463 circumcising¦16463 every¦16465 male¦16467 among you,
\v 16 Then¦16469 we'd¦16469 give¦16469 our¦16472 daughters to¦16473 you¦16473 \add to marry\add*, and¦16474 we'd¦16477 take¦16477 your daughters for¦16479 us¦16479 \add to marry\add*. And¦16480 we'd¦16480 settle¦16480 among you¦16481, and¦16482 we¦16482 \add all\add* would¦16482 become¦16482 one¦16484 \add united\add* people¦16483.
\v 17 \add But\add* if¦16486 you¦16489 all won't¦16488 \add agree\add* to¦16490 get circumcised¦16491, then¦16492 we'll¦16492 \add just\add* take¦16492 \add Dinah\add* and¦16496 go¦16496.”
\p
\v 18 \add This idea\add* \add ≈pleased¦16498\add* Hamor¦16501 and¦16502 \add *his¦16503\add* son¦16504,
\v 19 \add ≈so¦16508\add* \add Shekem\add* didn't¦16508 delay¦16510 \add implementing the plan\add* because¦16514 he¦16519 was¦16520 the most honoured¦16520 son in his¦16523 father's¦16523 household¦16522, and he was so delighted¦16515 with Yacob's¦16518 daughter¦16516.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦16525\add* Hamor¦16526 and¦16527 Shekem¦16527 went¦16525 to¦16529 \add the city elders at\add* the¦16531 gate¦16531 of¦16531 their¦16532 city¦16532, and¦16533 they¦16533 spoke¦16533 to¦16534 them, saying¦16538,
\v 21 “These¦16541 men¦16540 are¦16542 peaceful¦16542 towards us¦16544, so¦16545 let¦16545 them¦16545 settle¦16545 in¦16546 the¦16546 land¦16546, and¦16547 let¦16547 them¦16547 trade in¦16547 it¦16548. And¦16549 look, the¦16549 land¦16549 \add is plenty wide enough for them as well\add*. We¦16558 can take¦16558 their daughters for¦16560 ourselves as wives¦16561, and¦16562 we¦16565 can give¦16565 our daughters to¦16566 them¦16566 \add to marry\add*.
\v 22 \add But\add* they'll only¦16568 consent to¦16572 settle¦16574 among us¦16572 and unite with¦16575 us¦16575 on this¦16570 \add condition\add*: we would¦16571 need to¦16576 circumcise¦16579 all¦16581 of¦16581 the males¦16583 amongst us, just¦16584 like¦16584 they're¦16585 circumcised¦16586.
\v 23 Won't¦16593 all of¦16588 their¦16588 livestock¦16588 and¦16589 their¦16589 property¦16589 and¦16590 all¦16590 their¦16592 animals¦16592 then belong to¦16594 us¦16594? \add So\add* let's¦16597 agree¦16597 with \add their condition\add* and¦16599 then they'll¦16599 settle¦16599 among us¦16600.”
\v 24 All \add the elders\add* at the city gate \add agreed with\add* Hamor¦16605 and¦16606 his¦16609 son¦16609 Shekem¦16608, and \add so\add* every¦16610 male¦16618 who¦16612 \add passed through\add* the¦16613 city gate was¦16615 circumcised¦16615.
\rem /s1 Dinah's Brothers Avenge Their Sister
\p
\v 25 Three days¦16626 later when \add all those men\add* were¦16628 in¦16629 pain¦16629 \add from the cutting\add*, two¦16631 of¦16631 Yacob's¦16635 sons¦16633, Simeon¦16636 and¦16637 Levi¦16637 who were Dinah's¦16639 brothers¦16638, took¦16630 their \add #swords¦16641\add* and¦16642 boldly attacked the¦16645 city¦16645 and¦16647 slaughtered¦16647 every¦16648 male¦16650,
\v 26 including¦16652 Hamor¦16654 and¦16655 his¦16658 son¦16658 Shekem. Then¦16663 they¦16663 retrieved Dinah¦16666 from¦16667 Shekem's¦16668 house¦16667 and¦16669 left¦16669 \add the city\add*.
\v 27 Then when Yacob's¦16672 \add other sons\add* discovered that¦16679 a slaughter \add had taken place\add*, they looted¦16677 the¦16678 city¦16678 because their¦16681 sister¦16681 had been violated—
\v 28 taking¦16701 flocks¦16685 and¦16686 herds¦16688 and¦16689 donkeys¦16691—anything the was¦16696 in¦16696 the city¦16696 or \add out\add* in¦16700 the¦16700 countryside¦16700.
\v 29 They captured their¦16712 women¦16715 and children and took¦16716 all their¦16707 wealth¦16707 and everything that¦16721 was¦16722 in¦16722 \add &their\add* \add #houses¦16722\add*.
\p
\v 30 \add Afterwards,\add* Yacob¦16725 scolded Simeon¦16728 and¦16729 Levi¦16731, saying¦16724, “You¦16732 \add two\add* have¦16732 \add made\add* trouble¦16732 for me¦16733 by¦16734 \add destroying my reputation with\add* those who live in the¦16736 land¦16736—the Canaanites¦16737 and the Perizzites. \add There's only a few of us\add*, and if they¦16742 gather¦16742 together to attack¦16744 me¦16744 \add and my household\add*, then¦16745 \add we'll\add* be¦16745 destroyed¦16745—me and¦16747 \add all\add* my¦16747 household¦16747.”
\p
\v 31 \add But\add* they¦16749 \add ≈responded¦16749\add*, “Should he¦16751 \add have gotten away with\add* treating our¦16754 sister¦16754 like¦16750 a¦16750 prostitute¦16750?”
\c 35
