\p
\v 5 Then¦16850 they¦16850 \add started their journey but\add* and¦16851 the¦16853 \add people of\add* the¦16857 cities¦16857 around¦16859 them¦16859 \add ≈were afraid\add* \add of Yacob's god\add* so¦16860 they didn't¦16860 \add attack them\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦16866\add* Yacob¦16867 and everyone with him \add eventually arrived\add* at Luz¦16868 in¦16870 the Canaan¦16871 region¦16870 (which¦16872 is¦16873 \add now named\add* Beyt¦16873-El¦16875).
\v 7 He¦16884 built¦16884 an¦16886 altar¦16886 there and¦16887 named¦16887 the place¦16888 ‘El¦16889 Beyt¦16890-El¦16892’ \add (which means ‘the god of Beyt-El’)\add*, because¦16893 God had¦16895 revealed¦16895 himself to¦16896 him¦16896 there when¦16898 he¦16898 was fleeing¦16898 from¦16899 his¦16900 brother¦16900 \add Esaw\add*.
\v 8 Then¦16902 Rebekah's¦16905 nurse¦16904 Deborah¦16903 died¦16902 and¦16906 was¦16906 buried¦16906 under¦16907 the oak tree below Beyt¦16908-El¦16910 \add so\add* he¦16913 named¦16914 \add the place\add* ‘Allon Bakut’ \add (which means ‘oak of weeping’)\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add Now that Yacob had left\add* Paddan¦16926-Aram¦16927 and \add come back to Beyt-El\add*, God¦16920 appeared¦16919 to¦16921 him \add there\add* again¦16924 and¦16928 blessed¦16928 him¦16929
\v 10 and¦16931 told¦16931 him¦16933, “Your name is¦16936 Yacob¦16936 \add but\add* you won't¦16937 be¦16939 called¦16939 Yacob¦16943 anymore. \add From now on,\add* you'll be¦16948 called¦16949 Yisra'el (‘Israel’).” So¦16950 \add again\add*\x + \xo 35:10: \xt Gen 32:28.\x* \add @God¦16950\add* called¦16950 \add him\add* Yisra'el¦16954.
\v 11 Then¦16956 God \add also told\add* him¦16957, “I'm¦16959 God¦16960 the provider. Be¦16962 fruitful¦16962 and¦16963 multiply¦16963. Out¦16971 of you will come a¦16964 nation¦16964 and¦16965 a¦16965 community of¦16965 nations¦16966, and¦16969 kings¦16969 will come from¦16970 your¦16970 \add descendants\add*,\x + \xo 35:11-12: \xt Gen 17:4-8.\x*
\v 12 and¦16973 I'll¦16984 give you the¦16975 land¦16975 that¦16976 I¦16977 gave¦16977 to¦16978 Abraham¦16978 and¦16979 to¦16979 Isaac¦16979, and \add in the future,\add* I'll¦16981 give¦16981 the land to¦16982 your¦16982 descendants¦16982 after¦16983 you¦16983.”
\v 13 After God¦16991 finished talking¦16995 to \add @Yacob\add*, he left him¦16996 and went \add back\add* up.
\v 14 Then¦16998 Yacob¦16999 set¦16998 up¦16998 a¦17000 stone¦17007 pillar¦17000 at¦17001 the place¦17001 where¦17002 \add @God¦17004\add* had¦17004 spoken¦17004 with¦17005 him¦17005, and¦17008 he¦17008 poured¦17008 a¦17010 drink¦17010 offering¦17010 over it, followed by oil¦17013,\x + \xo 35:14-15: \xt Gen 28:18-19.\x*
\v 15 and¦17015 \add *he¦17016\add* named¦17019 that place¦17020 ‘Beyt¦17026-El¦17028’ \add (which means ‘God's house’) because\add* God¦17025 had¦17022 spoken¦17022 to him¦17023 there¦17024.
