\p
\v 1 Yisra'el \add !(Israel/Yacob/Jacob)\add* lived¦17818 in¦17820 the¦17821 area where his¦17822 father¦17822 \add Yitshak\add* had stayed, in¦17823 the Canaan¦17824 region.
\v 2 This is¦17828 \add the record of\add* \add *his¦17829\add* descendants:
\p When¦17830 Yosef¦17830 \add !(Joseph¦17830)\add* was¦17831 seventeen, he¦17837 was¦17837 shepherding¦17838 the \add #flocks¦17842\add* with¦17839 his¦17841 brothers¦17841. He¦17843 was¦17844 \add younger than his brothers\add* who were the¦17847 sons¦17847 of¦17847 his father's \add slave\add* wives¦17853 Bilhah¦17848 and¦17849 Zilpah¦17852. \add One day\add* Yosef¦17856 gave a \add tell-tale\add* bad¦17860 report¦17859 about¦17859 them to¦17861 their father.
\p
\v 3 \add Now\add* Yisra'el¦17865 loved¦17866 Yosef¦17869 more than¦17870 all¦17870 of¦17872 his¦17872 \add other\add* sons¦17872 because¦17873 he was¦17875 \add born to him when he was already old\add*, so¦17880 he¦17880 made¦17880 a¦17882 multicoloured robe¦17882 for him.
\v 4 \add When\add* his brothers saw¦17885 that¦17887 their¦17891 father¦17891 loved¦17890 \add @Yosef\add* more than¦17892 all¦17892 of¦17894 his¦17894 brothers, they¦17895 hated¦17895 him¦17896 and¦17897 couldn't \add make themselves say anything nice\add* to¦17899 him¦17899.
