\v 5 \add One night\add* Yosef¦17903 had a¦17904 dream¦17904, and¦17905 he¦17905 told¦17905 his¦17906 brothers¦17906 about¦17906 it, \add but\add* that made them hate¦17909 him¦17910 even more.
\v 6 He¦17912 \add ≈told¦17912\add* them¦17913, “Please¦17916 \add listen about\add* this¦17918 dream¦17917 that¦17919 I¦17920 \add had\add*:
\v 7 See¦17922, we¦17923 were¦17924 \add tying up bundles of grain stalks\add* in¦17926 the¦17926 middle¦17926 of a field¦17927, and¦17928 wow¦17928, my¦17930 bundle got up and¦17931 stood¦17933 upright¦17933. Then¦17934 \add would you believe it\add*, your bundles gathered¦17935 around¦17935 and¦17937 bowed¦17937 down¦17937 to¦17938 my¦17938 \add one\add*.”
\p
\v 8 “Will¦17944 you¦17944 really reign¦17944 over¦17945 us¦17945?” his¦17942 brothers¦17942 \add retorted\add*. “\add Do you think\add* you'll really¦17948 rule over¦17950 us¦17950?” \add So\add* they¦17951 continued¦17940 to¦17953 hate¦17953 him¦17954 even more because of his¦17957 dreams¦17957 and¦17958 because of¦17960 \add what he said\add*.
