\v 16 “I'm¦18084 \add ≈looking¦18085 for¦18085\add* my¦18083 brothers¦18083,” he answered¦18080. “Please¦18088 tell¦18086 me¦18089 where¦18090 they're¦18091 \add ≈looking after\add* \add our flocks\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “They've¦18096 left¦18096 here¦18097,” the¦18095 man¦18095 responded. “I¦18099 heard¦18099 them¦18099 say¦18100, ‘Let's¦18101 go¦18101 to¦18102 Dothan¦18102.’ ”
\rem /s1 Joseph Sold into Slavery
\p So¦18103 Yosef¦18104 continued on after¦18105 his¦18106 brothers¦18106 and¦18107 found¦18107 them¦18107 at¦18108 Dotan¦18108,
\v 18 \add but\add* they¦18110 saw¦18110 him¦18111 from¦18112 a¦18112 distance¦18112 and¦18113 before¦18113 he¦18114 \add got close\add* to¦18115 them¦18115, they¦18116 \add made plans among themselves\add* to¦18118 kill¦18118 him¦18118.
\v 19 ⇔“Look, that¦18128 master¦18126 \add dreamer\add* is¦18129 coming¦18129,” they said¦18120 to each¦18121 other.
\v 20 “\add Here's our chance to\add* kill¦18134 him¦18134 and¦18135 throw¦18135 \add his body\add* into¦18136 one¦18136 of¦18136 the¦18137 pits¦18137 \add around here\add*. We'll¦18138 say¦18138 that a \add wild\add* animal¦18139 \add attacked\add* him¦18141. \em Then¦18142\em* we'll¦18142 see¦18142 what¦18143 his¦18146 dreams¦18146 \add turn into\add*.”
\p
\v 21 But¦18148 Reuben¦18149 heard¦18148 \add what they were saying\add*, and¦18150 he¦18150 \add tried to\add* rescue¦18150 \add @Yosef\add* \add by insisting\add*, “Let's¦18154 not \add take\add* his life¦18155.”
\v 22 “Don't¦18161 shed¦18163 blood¦18165,” \add *he\add* continued¦18157. “Throw¦18166 him¦18167 into¦18168 \add that\add* pit¦18170 in the wilderness¦18173, but¦18174 don't¦18175 \add wound\add* him¦18179.” \add He said this\add* because he was planning to¦18181 rescue¦18181 \add @Yosef¦18182\add* \add later\add* and return¦18184 him¦18184 \add home\add* to¦18185 \add their\add* father¦18187.
\v 23 \add ≈So\add* when Yosef¦18193 \add reached\add* his¦18196 brothers¦18196, they¦18197 \add grabbed him and ripped\add* off the¦18206 coloured robe¦18206 that¦18208 \add he was wearing\add*.
\v 24 Then¦18211 they¦18211 took¦18211 him¦18211 and¦18212 \add dropped\add* him¦18213 into¦18214 the¦18214 pit¦18214. (The¦18215 pit¦18215 was¦18216 empty¦18216 with no water¦18219 in \add the bottom\add*).
\p
\v 25 Then¦18221 they¦18221 sat down to¦18222 eat¦18222, and \add a bit later when they looked up\add*, look¦18228, \add there was\add* a¦18229 caravan¦18229 of¦18229 Yishma'elites coming¦18231 \add towards them\add*. \add They had left\add* Gilead¦18232 carrying¦18234 \add #spices¦18235\add* and¦18236 balm¦18236 and¦18237 myrrh¦18237 on their¦18233 camels¦18233 that they¦18238 were¦18238 going to¦18239 take¦18239 down¦18239 to Egypt¦18240.
\v 26 Then¦18242 Yehudah¦18243 \add !(Judah¦18243)\add* said¦18242 to¦18244 his¦18246 brothers¦18246, “What¦18247 will we gain¦18249 if we¦18251 kill¦18251 our¦18254 brother¦18254 and¦18255 cover¦18255 up his¦18258 blood¦18258?
\v 27 Let's¦18261 sell¦18261 him¦18261 to¦18262 \add these\add* Ishmaelites¦18262 \add so we won't be guilty of killing\add* him¦18268. \add After all,\add* he's¦18273 our brother¦18271—our¦18271 \add own\add* flesh¦18272 \add and blood\add*.” And his¦18275 brothers¦18275 \add agreed\add*.
\v 28 \add ≈So¦18277\add* \add when\add* the Midianite traders¦18280 came past, \add the brothers\add* pulled¦18281 Yosef up and¦18282 lifted¦18282 him out of the¦18288 pit¦18288 and¦18289 sold¦18289 \add *him¦18292\add* to¦18293 the Ishmaelites¦18293 for¦18294 twenty¦18294 \add pieces\add* of silver¦18295. Then¦18296 \add the traders took\add* Yosef¦18299 \add onwards with them\add* to Mitsrayim¦18300.\x + \xo 37:28: \xt Acts 7:9.\x*
