\p
\v 1 \add Around that time\add*, Yehudah¦18430 \add !(Judah¦18430)\add* went down \add the hills\add* from¦18431 \add where\add* his¦18432 brothers¦18432 \add were\add* and¦18433 settled near an¦18437 Adullamite¦18437 man¦18436 named¦18438 Hirah¦18439.
\v 2 There¦18443 Yehudah¦18444 saw¦18441 the daughter¦18445 of¦18445 a¦18448 Canaanite¦18448 man¦18447 named¦18449 Shua¦18450, and¦18451 he¦18451 took¦18451 her¦18451 \add as a wife\add*. He¦18452 \add slept with\add* her¦18453
\v 3 and¦18455 she¦18455 got¦18455 pregnant¦18455 and¦18456 \add in due course\add*, gave¦18456 birth¦18456 to a¦18457 son¦18457 who \add @Yehudah\add* named¦18461 Er¦18462.
\v 4 Then¦18464 she¦18464 got¦18464 pregnant¦18464 again¦18465 and¦18466 gave¦18466 birth¦18466 a¦18467 \add another\add* son¦18467, and¦18468 she¦18468 named¦18468 him Onan¦18472.
\v 5 Then¦18474 she¦18474 \add got pregnant yet again\add* and¦18476 gave¦18476 birth¦18476 to a¦18477 \add third\add* son¦18477, and¦18478 she¦18478 named¦18478 him Shelah¦18482. (\add @Yehudah¦18483\add* was¦18483 in¦18484 Kezib¦18484 when¦18485 she¦18485 \add Onan was born\add*.)
\p
\v 6 \add In due course,\add* Yehudah¦18489 took¦18488 a¦18490 wife¦18490 for¦18491 Er¦18491 his¦18492 firstborn¦18492, and¦18493 her¦18493 name¦18493 was¦18494 Tamar¦18494.
\v 7 But¦18496 Er¦18497 was evil¦18500 in¦18501 Yahweh's eyes¦18501, so Yahweh¦18502 killed¦18503 him¦18503.
\v 8 Then¦18506 Yehudah¦18507 said¦18506 to¦18508 Onan¦18508, “Go¦18509 to¦18510 your¦18513 brother's¦18513 wife¦18512 and¦18514 perform¦18514 your \add brotherly\add* duty to her¦18515 \add to\add* produce¦18516 \add children\add* for¦18518 your brother.”
\v 9 However, Onan¦18521 knew¦18520 that¦18522 \add any children\add* wouldn't be¦18528 his, so \add whenever\add* he¦18531 \add slept with\add* his¦18535 brother's¦18535 wife¦18534, he¦18536 spilled \add his semen\add* on the ground¦18537 so that he wouldn't give¦18539 \add children\add* to¦18542 his \add late\add* brother.
\v 10 \add But\add* Yahweh¦18546 \add considered\add* what he¦18548 did¦18548 to be evil¦18544, so¦18549 he¦18549 killed¦18549 him also¦18550.
\v 11 Then¦18554 Yehudah¦18555 \add ≈told¦18554\add* his¦18557 daughter-in-law¦18557 Tamar, “Remain¦18558 a¦18559 widow¦18559 in your¦18562 father's¦18562 house until¦18563 my¦18567 son¦18567 Shelah¦18566 grows¦18565 up¦18565.” \add This was\add* because¦18568 he'd¦18569 said¦18569, “So that he¦18572 doesn't also¦18573 die¦18572 like¦18576 his¦18576 brothers¦18576!” So¦18577 Tamar¦18578 went¦18577 and¦18579 lived¦18579 in the¦18580 house¦18580 of¦18580 her¦18581 father¦18581.
\p
\v 12 \add A long time afterwards\add*, Yehudah's wife¦18589 (Shua's¦18588 daughter¦18586) died¦18585. \add After\add* Yehudah \add had finished mourning\add*, he¦18592 and¦18594 his¦18598 friend Hirah¦18600 (the¦18602 Adullamite¦18602) went to¦18603 Timnah¦18603 to \add where\add* the men were shearing¦18597 his sheep¦18598.
\v 13 Then¦18605 Tamar¦18606 was¦18605 told¦18605, “Look, your¦18609 father-in-law¦18609 is¦18610 going¦18610 to¦18611 Timnah¦18611 to¦18612 shear¦18612 his¦18613 sheep¦18613.”
\v 14 \add ≈So¦18615\add* she¦18615 \add changed out of\add* her¦18617 widow's¦18617 clothes¦18616 and¦18619 covered¦18619 herself with¦18620 a veil¦18620 and¦18621 wrapped¦18621 herself¦18621 \add up\add*. Then¦18622 she¦18622 sat¦18622 at¦18623 the¦18623 entrance¦18623 of¦18623 Enaim¦18624 which¦18625 is¦18626 on¦18626 the¦18628 road¦18628 to¦18629 Timnah¦18629. \add She was doing this\add* because¦18630 she¦18631 had¦18631 seen¦18631 that¦18632 Shelah¦18635 had¦18634 grown¦18634 up¦18634, but¦18636 she hadn't been¦18639 given¦18639 to¦18640 him¦18640 as a¦18641 wife¦18641.
\p
\v 15 \add In due course,\add* Yehudah¦18644 saw¦18643 her¦18643 and because¦18647 she¦18648 had¦18648 covered¦18648 her¦18649 face¦18649, he thought¦18645 she was a¦18646 prostitute¦18646.
\v 16 \add ≈So¦18651\add* he¦18651 turned¦18651 to¦18652 her¦18652 beside the¦18655 road¦18655 and¦18656 asked¦18656, “Please¦18659 let¦18660 me¦18660 \add lie with\add* you¦18661,” because¦18662 he¦18664 didn't¦18663 know¦18664 that¦18665 she was¦18666 his¦18666 daughter-in-law¦18666.
\p “What¦18669 will¦18671 you¦18671 give¦18671 me \add in exchange\add*?” she \add asked\add*.
