\v 18 “What¦18697 pledge¦18698 \add should\add* I¦18700 give¦18700 you¦18702?” he \add asked\add*.
\p “Your¦18704 signet \add ring\add* and¦18705 \add its\add* cord¦18705, and¦18706 your¦18706 staff¦18706 that¦18707 \add you're holding\add*.” \add So\add* he¦18709 \add handed\add* them¦18709 to¦18711 her¦18711 and¦18712 went¦18712 and lay with her¦18713, and¦18714 she¦18714 became¦18714 pregnant¦18714 \add as a result\add*.
\v 19 Then¦18717 \add @Tamar¦18717\add* got up and¦18718 left¦18718, and¦18719 she¦18719 took¦18719 off her¦18720 veil¦18720 and¦18722 put¦18722 her¦18724 widow's¦18724 clothes¦18723 \add back\add* on.
\p
\v 20 Then¦18726 Yehudah¦18727 sent¦18726 his¦18733 friend the¦18734 Adullamite¦18734 to¦18735 take¦18735 the young goat¦18731 and get the pledge¦18736 back from¦18737 the¦18738 woman¦18738, but¦18739 he¦18740 couldn't find¦18740 her¦18740,
\v 21 \add ≈so¦18742\add* he¦18742 asked¦18742 \add some of the local\add* men¦18745, “Where's¦18748 the¦18749 temple prostitute¦18749 who was¦18751 at¦18751 Enaim¦18751 beside the¦18754 road¦18754?”
\p \add But\add* they¦18755 answered¦18755, “There's \add never\add* been¦18758 a¦18760 temple prostitute¦18760 \add around here\add*.”
