\v 22 \add ≈So¦18762\add* \add Hirah\add* returned¦18762 to¦18763 Yehudah¦18765 and¦18766 \add ≈told¦18766 him\add*, “I¦18768 couldn't find¦18768 her¦18768. \add What's more\add*, the¦18770 men¦18770 of¦18770 the¦18771 place¦18771 said¦18772 that there hasn't been¦18775 a¦18777 temple prostitute¦18777 at that place.”
\p
\v 23 “\add Oh well,\add*” said¦18779 Yehudah¦18780. “Let¦18781 her¦18781 \add keep those\add* things for¦18783 herself so that¦18790 we¦18785 don't¦18792 become¦18785 a laughingstock¦18786. Anyway, I¦18788 \add did my duty by sending the goat\add*, but¦18791 you couldn't find¦18793 her¦18793.”
\p
\v 24 About¦18797 three¦18797 months¦18799 later, Yehudah was¦18800 told¦18800, “Your¦18805 daughter-in-law¦18805 Tamar¦18804 has¦18803 prostituted¦18803 herself, and¦18806 \add not only that\add*, she's¦18808 pregnant¦18808 from doing it¦18810.”
\p “Bring¦18812 her¦18812 out¦18812 and let her be¦18813 burnt¦18813 \add to death\add*.” Yehudah \add demanded\add*.
