\p
\v 1 \add Meanwhile (up in the Canaan region),\add* Yacob¦20677 \add heard\add* that¦20678 there¦20679 was¦20679 grain¦20681 \add available\add* in¦20682 Egypt¦20682, so¦20683 \add he\add* said¦20683 to¦20685 his¦20685 sons¦20685, “Why are¦20687 you¦20687 \add just standing there\add* looking¦20687 at¦20687 each other?
\v 2 Listen, I've¦20691 heard¦20691 that¦20692 \add they're selling\add* grain¦20695 in¦20696 Egypt¦20696. Go¦20697 down¦20697 there and¦20700 buy¦20700 some for¦20702 us¦20702 so¦20704 that¦20704 we \add won't just starve to death here\add*.”\x + \xo 42:2: \xt Acts 7:12.\x*
\v 3 \add ≈So¦20708\add* ten¦20712 of¦20711 Yosef's¦20711 brothers¦20709 \add travelled\add* down¦20708 to Egypt¦20715 to buy¦20713 grain¦20713,
\v 4 \add but\add* Yacob¦20725 wouldn't send¦20724 Benyamin¦20719 (Yosef's¦20721 \add youngest\add* brother¦20720) with¦20726 \add the others\add*, because¦20729 he¦20730 said¦20730, “I don't¦20722 want any harm¦20734 to come¦20733 to¦20733 him¦20733.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦20736\add* Yisra'el's¦20738 sons¦20737 \add found themselves\add* among \add many others\add* who¦20741 \add went\add* to¦20739 buy¦20739 grain¦20739, because¦20742 the¦20745 famine¦20745 was \add also throughout\add* the Canaan¦20747 \add region\add*.
\v 6 \add Now\add* Yosef¦20749 was¦20751 the¦20751 governor¦20751 over¦20752 \add all of Egypt\add* and he¦20755 \add was the one there\add* who¦20756 was selling¦20756 grain¦20756 to¦20757 all¦20757 the¦20759 people¦20759. So¦20761 Yosef's¦20763 brothers¦20762 \add approached\add* and¦20764 bowed¦20764 down¦20764 to¦20766 him¦20766 with their noses to the¦20768 ground¦20768.
\v 7 \add When\add* Yosef¦20771 saw¦20770 his¦20774 brothers¦20774, he¦20775 recognized¦20775 them¦20775 and¦20776 acted¦20776 like¦20776 a¦20776 stranger¦20776 to¦20777 them¦20777, and¦20778 he¦20778 spoke¦20778 harshly¦20780 with¦20779 them \add (through an interpreter)\add*, “Where¦20783 \add are you lot from\add*?”
\p “From¦20786 the¦20786 land¦20786 of¦20786 Canaan¦20787 to¦20788 buy¦20788 food¦20790,” they \add ≈answered\add*.
\p
\v 8 Yosef¦20793 had recognised¦20792 his¦20796 brothers¦20796, but¦20797 they hadn't recognised¦20799 him¦20799,
\v 9 and¦20801 \add just then\add* \add *he¦20802\add* remembered¦20801 the¦20804 dreams¦20804 that¦20805 he¦20806 had¦20806 dreamed¦20806 about¦20815 them¦20807, \add so\add* he¦20808 said¦20808 to¦20809 them¦20809, “You are¦20810 spies¦20810. You've¦20817 \add all\add* come¦20817 to \add discover any weak points in this country's defences\add*.”\x + \xo 42:9: \xt Gen 37:5-10.\x*
\p
\v 10 “No¦20821, my¦20822 master¦20822,” they \add ≈answered¦20819\add*. “Your¦20823 servants¦20823 have¦20824 \add only\add* come¦20824 to¦20825 buy¦20825 food¦20827.
\v 11 We're \add all\add* sons¦20830 of¦20830 \add the same\add* man¦20831. We're¦20834 \add being\add* honest¦20835. Your¦20840 servants¦20840 are¦20839 not spies¦20841.”
\p
\v 12 “No¦20845, you've¦20850 definitely \add all\add* come¦20850 \add here\add* to¦20851 see¦20851 \add where\add* \add &our\add* \add land is vulnerable\add*,” \add @Yosef\add* \add insisted\add*.
\p
\v 13 “Your¦20856 servants¦20856 are twelve brothers¦20857,” they protested. “We're¦20859 \add all\add* sons¦20860 of¦20860 one¦20863 man¦20863 in¦20864 the Canaan¦20865 \add region\add*. \add It's all true\add*—the¦20867 youngest is¦20868 \add home\add* with¦20868 our¦20870 father¦20870, and¦20872 one¦20872 \add has passed away\add*.”
\p
\v 14 “\add Yes,\add* it's¦20875 just as I said¦20875,” retorted Yosef¦20877. “You're¦20881 spies¦20883!
\v 15 \add But\add* this¦20886 is¦20887 how we'll test¦20887 you all: On Far'oh's¦20889 life¦20888, you¦20892 won't \add ever\add* leave¦20892 this place unless your youngest brother¦20898 comes¦20897 here¦20900.
\v 16 \add Select\add* one¦20904 among you to go and get¦20905 your¦20908 brother¦20908, and¦20909 \add the rest of\add* you¦20909 will be \add imprisoned\add*. Then \add we'll\add* \add ≈find out\add* \add if you've all been telling the truth\add*. And¦20915 if¦20915 not¦20917, on Far'oh's¦20919 life¦20918, you're certainly spies¦20921.”
\v 17 Then¦20924 he¦20924 had them¦20925 \add ≈locked up\add* together for three¦20929 days¦20930.
\p
\v 18 On the¦20936 third¦20936 day¦20935, Yosef¦20934 told them, “I'm a man who reveres God. So if you do¦20938 \add exactly\add* what I say¦20932, I'll let you live¦20939.
\v 19 If¦20946 you are¦20948 \add actually\add* honest¦20948, leave one¦20951 of your¦20954 \add #brothers¦20950\add* \add in prison here\add*, and¦20955 you¦20955 \add others\add* go¦20956 and take¦20957 grain¦20958 back \add to feed\add* your¦20960 families¦20960.
\v 20 Then¦20962 \add when\add* you¦20966 will¦20966 bring¦20966 me¦20967 your¦20969 youngest brother¦20964 so¦20968 that¦20968 \add I can verify your statements\add*, then¦20970 you¦20971 won't¦20970 die¦20971.” So¦20972 they¦20972 \add agreed\add*,
\v 21 saying¦20976 to each¦20977 other \add (in Hebrew)\add*, “We are¦20982 truly guilty¦20982 concerning our¦20987 brother \add Yosef\add*, because we¦20989 saw¦20989 the¦20990 distress¦20990 of¦20990 his¦20991 soul¦20991 when¦20992 he¦20992 pleaded with us¦20993, but¦20994 we¦20995 didn't¦20994 \add ≈take any notice\add*. \add That's why\add* this¦21002 \add predicament has happened to\add* us.”
\p
\v 22 “Didn't¦21008 I¦21009 \add beg\add* you¦21010 \add all\add* not to sin¦21015 against¦21016 the lad?” Reuben¦21005 spoke up. “But¦21017 you¦21018 wouldn't listen¦21018, so¦21019 now, see, \add now we're having to account for\add* his¦21021 blood¦21021.”\x + \xo 42:22: \xt Gen 37:21-22.\x*
\v 23 (\add But\add* they¦21025 didn't¦21026 know¦21027 that¦21028 Yosef¦21030 understood them¦21033, because \add he and them had been speaking through an interpreter\add*.)
\v 24 \add @Yosef¦21035\add* turned¦21035 away¦21035 from¦21036 them¦21036 \add briefly so they couldn't see his tears\add*, then he turned¦21038 back toward them¦21039 and¦21040 spoke¦21040 to¦21041 them¦21041. Then¦21042 he¦21042 had Simeon¦21046 \add separated\add* from \add the group\add* and¦21047 tied¦21047 up in front of¦21049 them.
\v 25 Then¦21051 Yosef¦21052 ordered \add his servants\add* and¦21053 they filled¦21053 their¦21056 bags with grain¦21057, and¦21058 he \add quietly\add* ordered them to¦21058 return¦21058 each¦21060 man's silver¦21059 \add back\add* to¦21061 his¦21063 sack¦21063 and¦21064 to¦21064 give¦21064 them¦21065 provisions¦21066 to¦21069 them¦21069 for the road.
\s1 Yosef's brothers return home
