\p \add After Yosef had provided for his brothers\add*,
\v 26 they¦21072 loaded their grain¦21075 onto their¦21075 donkeys¦21078 and¦21079 departed¦21079.
\v 27 At¦21090 a lodging place¦21090 \add that night\add*, one¦21083 \add of them\add* opened¦21082 his sack to feed his¦21089 donkey¦21089 and¦21091 \add to his horror\add*, he¦21091 saw¦21091 his¦21094 silver¦21094 inside the top of the sack¦21099.
\v 28 “My¦21106 silver's¦21106 been¦21105 returned¦21105,” he told his¦21104 brothers¦21104, “and¦21107 it's \add right here\add* in¦21109 my¦21109 sack¦21109!” Then their¦21111 \add ≈stomachs tightened\add*, and trembling¦21112, they¦21112 \add ≈asked\add* each¦21113 other, “What's¦21118 this¦21120 that God's¦21122 doing¦21121 to¦21123 us¦21123?”
\p
\v 29 \add When\add* they¦21125 \add got home\add* to¦21126 Yacob¦21128 their¦21129 father¦21129 in Canaan¦21131, they¦21132 told¦21132 him¦21133 everything that¦21137 had¦21137 happened¦21137 to¦21137 them¦21138,
\v 30 “\add This\add* man¦21142, the¦21143 master¦21143 of¦21143 \add Egypt\add*, spoke¦21141 harshly¦21146 to us¦21145 and¦21147 treated us¦21148 as¦21149 if we were spying¦21149 out¦21149 \add &his¦21152\add* \add country\add*,
\v 31 but¦21154 we¦21154 told¦21154 him¦21155, ‘We're¦21159 honest¦21156—we're¦21157 not¦21158 spies¦21160.
\v 32 We're¦21165 twelve brothers¦21166, the sons¦21167 of¦21167 our¦21168 father¦21168. One¦21169 is¦21170 \add no longer\add* alive, and the¦21171 youngest¦21171 is¦21173 with¦21173 our father today \add back\add* in¦21176 Canaan¦21177.’
\v 33 Then¦21179 \add that\add* man¦21181 told¦21179 us¦21180, ‘\add I'll\add* \add ≈find out\add* \add if you're honest\add*: Leave¦21191 one¦21181 of your¦21189 \add #brothers¦21189\add* with¦21192 me¦21192, and¦21193 take¦21197 grain for your¦21196 families¦21196 and¦21198 go¦21198.
\v 34 Then¦21200 bring¦21200 me¦21205 your youngest brother so¦21206 that¦21206 I'll¦21206 know¦21206 you're not¦21208 spies¦21209—that¦21211 you're¦21213 \add telling the truth\add*. Then I'll¦21217 \add release\add* your brother and¦21219 you¦21222 can trade \add here freely\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 35 Then¦21224 \add when\add* they¦21225 \add started\add* emptying¦21226 their¦21227 sacks¦21227, wow¦21228, each¦21230 man's¦21230 pouch of¦21231 silver¦21233 was¦21234 inside his¦21234 sack¦21234. \add When the brothers\add* and¦21235 their¦21241 father¦21241 saw¦21235 their¦21239 pouches of silver, they were¦21242 afraid¦21242.
\v 36 “You've \add deprived\add* me \add of another son\add*,” Yacob¦21246 \add exclaimed\add*. Yosef¦21250 is¦21251 \add gone\add*! Simeon's¦21252 \add gone\add*! And¦21254 \add then you want to take\add* Benyamin¦21256 \add as well\add*! \add Why's everything going so wrong for\add* me¦21258?”
\v 37 Then¦21262 Reuben¦21263 \add offered\add* to¦21264 his¦21266 father¦21266, “You¦21272 can kill¦21272 my two¦21270 sons¦21271 if¦21273 I¦21276 don't¦21275 bring¦21276 \add @Benyamin¦21276\add* \add back\add* to¦21277 you¦21277. \add Let me take responsibility for him\add*, and¦21283 I'll¦21284 \add make sure that he\add* returns to¦21285 you¦21285.”
\v 38 “My¦21291 son¦21291 will¦21290 \em not\em* go¦21290 with¦21292 you,” \add @Yacob\add* countered, “because¦21293 his¦21295 brother¦21295 is dead, and¦21297 he¦21297 alone¦21298 is¦21299 left. And¦21300 if harm¦21301 were to¦21300 meet him¦21300 on¦21302 the road that¦21303 you're¦21304 going¦21304 on¦21306, then¦21307 you'd¦21307 bring my¦21310 grey¦21310 head down to the grave in¦21311 grief¦21311.”
\c 43
\s1 Yosef's brothers bring Benyamin to Egypt
\rem /s1 Joseph's Brothers Return to Egypt with Benjamin; The Brothers Come Again, Bringing Benjamin; The Brothers Return to Egypt; The Second Journey to Egypt
\p
\v 1 \add However,\add* the¦21314 famine¦21314 in the region was¦21315 \add still\add* very severe,
\v 2 \add ≈so\add* when they'd¦21320 \add used up all\add* the¦21324 grain¦21324 that¦21325 they'd¦21326 brought¦21326 from¦21327 Egypt¦21327, their¦21330 father¦21330 \add instructed\add* them, “Go¦21331 back¦21331 \add there and\add* buy¦21332 \add some\add* food¦21337 for¦21334 us¦21334.”
\p
\v 3 \add But\add* Yehudah¦21341 \add challenged\add* him, “\add That\add* man¦21346 \add ≈told¦21347 us that he won't¦21348 even see¦21350 us\add* unless \add our\add* brother¦21353 is¦21354 with¦21354 \add us\add*.
\v 4 ⇔We¦21364 can \add only\add* go¦21364 \add there\add* to buy¦21365 food¦21367 for you if¦21356 you'll¦21358 \add agree to\add* send¦21359 our \add youngest\add* brother¦21362 with¦21363 us¦21363.
\v 5 If¦21369 you¦21371 don't¦21373, \add it's not even worth going, because that\add* man¦21377 \add clearly told us that he won't even see us\add* unless \add our\add* brother¦21385 is¦21386 with¦21386 \add us\add*.
\p
\v 6 “Why¦21390 did¦21391 you¦21391 all treat me¦21392 badly by telling the man¦21394 you¦21396 have \add a younger\add* brother¦21397?” \add their father\add* Yisra'el¦21389 asked¦21388.
\p
\v 7 “The¦21403 man¦21403 \add kept asking\add* about us¦21404 and¦21405 our¦21405 relatives,” they answered¦21399. “\add ≡He asked\add*, ‘Is¦21408 your¦21408 father¦21408 still¦21407 alive¦21409? Do you¦21411 have another brother¦21412?’ \add We just answered what he asked\add*. How could we¦21413 possibly¦21422 know that¦21424 he¦21425 would¦21425 \add insist that we bring our youngest brother there\add*?”
\p
\v 8 Then¦21431 Yehudah¦21432 said¦21431 to¦21433 his¦21436 father¦21436, “\add Entrust\add* the¦21438 young¦21438 man¦21438 to me¦21439, and¦21440 we'll¦21440 \add pack\add* up and¦21441 go¦21441 so¦21442 that¦21442 both¦21445 we¦21447 and you¦21450 and our¦21453 little¦21453 ones¦21453 will live¦21442 and¦21443 not¦21443 die¦21444.
\v 9 I myself will¦21456 guarantee¦21456 him. \add If anything happens to him, you can charge it to me\add*. If¦21459 I¦21462 don't¦21461 \add get\add* him¦21462 \add safely\add* back to¦21463 you¦21463, then I'll \add personally\add* carry the¦21470 blame¦21466 \add for the rest of my life\add*.
\v 10 \add If we hadn't sat around here doing nothing for so long\add*, certainly by now¦21477 we¦21478 could have¦21478 \add been there and back\add* twice!”
\p
\v 11 “\add Well, if that's our only choice\add*,” their¦21485 father¦21485 \add acceded\add*, “then¦21490 do this¦21491: Take¦21493 some¦21494 of¦21494 the¦21494 best¦21494 produce¦21494 \add from around here\add* in¦21496 your¦21496 bags, and¦21497 take¦21497 it down¦21497 to¦21498 the man¦21498 as a¦21499 gift¦21499: a¦21500 little¦21500 balm¦21501, a¦21502 little¦21502 honey¦21503, \add #spices¦21504\add* and¦21505 myrrh¦21505, \add and some\add* pistachio¦21506 nuts¦21506 and¦21507 almonds¦21507.
\v 12 And¦21509 take double¦21510 the \add amount of\add* silver, because you must repay the silver that¦21516 was¦21516 returned¦21516 in¦21517 the¦21517 \add tops\add* of¦21517 your¦21518 sacks¦21518. Perhaps¦21521 it was¦21522 a¦21522 mistake¦21522.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦21525\add* take¦21528 your¦21527 brother¦21527 and¦21529 \add go and\add* return¦21530 to¦21531 the¦21533 man¦21533.
\v 14 May the provider God¦21535 Almighty¦21536 \add cause\add* the¦21541 man¦21541 to treat you kindly, and may he send your¦21546 other¦21547 brother¦21546 and¦21548 Benyamin¦21550 \add back\add* with you. And¦21551 \add as for me\add*, if I \add lose another son\add*, I'll \add just have to mourn him\add*.”
\p
\v 15 \add ≈So¦21556\add* the \add brothers\add* took the \add #gifts¦21560\add* and¦21562 double¦21562 the \add amount of\add* silver. Then¦21567 \add taking\add* Benyamin¦21569, they \add travelled\add* down¦21571 to Egypt¦21572 and¦21573 \add presented themselves\add* to¦21574 Yosef¦21575.
\v 16 \add When\add* Yosef¦21578 saw¦21577 Benyamin¦21582 with¦21579 them¦21579, he¦21583 told¦21583 \add his head house-servant\add*, “Take¦21588 \add these\add* men¦21591 to¦21592 the¦21592 house¦21592, and¦21593 slaughter an animal and¦21595 prepare¦21595 a meal, because¦21596 \add they'll\add* eat¦21598 with¦21597 me¦21597 at¦21600 noon¦21600.”
\v 17 The¦21603 man¦21603 did what \add he'd\add* been instructed and¦21607 brought¦21607 the men¦21611 to¦21612 Yosef's¦21613 house¦21612.
\p
\v 18 \add But\add* the \add brothers\add* were¦21615 afraid¦21615 when they¦21618 \add found out that they'd been\add* brought¦21618 to \add wait outside\add* Yosef's¦21620 house¦21619, and¦21621 said¦21621 \add to each other\add*, “We must have been brought \add here\add* because¦21617 of¦21624 the¦21625 silver¦21625 that¦21626 was returned¦21626 in¦21627 our¦21627 sacks¦21627 the first time. \add He wants to overpower us, then arrest\add* us¦21632 and¦21633 \add confiscate\add* our¦21640 donkeys¦21640 and¦21635 take¦21635 us¦21636 as slaves¦21637.”
\rem /s1 A Feast at Joseph's Palace
\v 19 \add ≈So¦21642\add* they¦21642 approached¦21642 the \add head servant\add* and¦21651 spoke¦21651 to¦21652 him¦21652 at the¦21653 entrance¦21653 of¦21653 the¦21654 house¦21654,
\v 20 \add explaining\add*, “Please, my¦21658 master¦21658, honestly, we¦21660 came¦21660 down¦21660 here the first time to¦21662 buy¦21662 food¦21664.
\v 21 \add But\add* when¦21666 we¦21669 \add got\add* to¦21670 \add &our¦21672\add* lodging¦21672 place¦21672 \add that evening\add*, we¦21673 opened¦21673 our¦21676 sacks¦21676 and¦21677 \add got a shock because\add* each¦21680 man's¦21680 silver was¦21681 in¦21681 the¦21681 \add top\add* of¦21681 his¦21682 sack¦21682—the full amount of our silver was there. So¦21685 we've¦21685 brought¦21685 it back¦21685 \add here on this trip\add*,
\v 22 plus¦21689 we've¦21691 brought¦21691 more silver to¦21693 buy¦21693 food¦21695. We¦21697 don't¦21696 know¦21697 who¦21698 put¦21700 \add that\add* silver¦21701 in¦21702 our¦21702 sacks¦21702.”
\v 23 \add But\add* he¦21704 said¦21704, “Peace¦21705 to¦21706 you¦21706—don't¦21707 be afraid¦21709. Your god and¦21711 the¦21711 god¦21711 of¦21711 your¦21712 father¦21712 has given¦21713 you¦21714 hidden¦21715 treasure¦21715 in¦21716 your¦21716 sacks¦21716—\add I received your previous payment\add*.” Then¦21720 he¦21720 brought¦21720 Simeon¦21724 out¦21720 to¦21721 them¦21721.
