\s1 Yacob's arrival in Egypt
\rem /s1 Jacob and His Family in Egypt; Jacob Settles in Goshen; Jacob's Family Arrives in Goshen
\p
\v 28 \add As they all approached Egypt, Yacob\add* sent¦23320 Yehudah¦23319 ahead¦23321 \add of the others\add* to¦23322 find out from Yosef¦23324 how to¦23325 get to¦23327 Goshen¦23327. \add As they all\add* arrived¦23328 in the Goshen¦23330 area,
\v 29 Yosef¦23333 \add hooked up\add* his¦23334 chariot¦23334 and¦23335 went to¦23336 meet¦23336 his¦23339 father¦23339 Yisra'el¦23338 \add *there¦23340\add*. He \add went up to his father, and hugged him for a long time as he cried\add*.
\v 30 “Now I can die¦23358,” Yisra'el¦23354 said¦23353 to¦23355 Yosef¦23357, “since I've¦23361 seen¦23361 your¦23364 face¦23364—\add seen\add* that¦23359 you're still¦23366 alive¦23367.”
\p
\v 31 Then¦23369 Yosef¦23370 spoke¦23369 to¦23371 his brothers and¦23374 to¦23374 his¦23377 father's¦23377 household, “I'll¦23378 go¦23378 and¦23379 report¦23379 to¦23380 Far'oh¦23380 and¦23381 \add explain\add* to¦23382 him¦23382 that my brothers and¦23384 my¦23386 father's¦23386 household who¦23387 were living in¦23388 Canaan¦23390 have¦23391 come¦23391 to¦23392 \add join\add* me¦23392.
\v 32 \add I'll tell him that you're\add* herders of¦23395 sheep¦23396—livestock¦23400 \add farmers\add*—and \add that you've\add* brought¦23408 \add %your\add* flocks¦23402 and¦23403 herds¦23403 and¦23404 everything that¦23406 \add you own\add*.
\v 33 \add ≈So\add* when Far'oh¦23415 calls for¦23414 you¦23414 and¦23416 \add asks what your work is\add*,
\v 34 then¦23421 you¦23421 should \add answer\add*, ‘Your¦23425 servants¦23425 have been livestock¦23423 men¦23422 from our¦23426 youth¦23426 and¦23427 until now¦23429, both¦23430 we¦23432 and¦23421 also¦23421 our¦23435 fathers¦23435,’ so that you¦23437 can settle¦23437 \add here\add* in¦23438 Goshen¦23439, because¦23440 Egyptians \add despise sheep herders\add*.”
\c 47
\rem /s1 Jacob Blesses Pharaoh
\p
\v 1 Then¦23449 went¦23449 Yosef¦23450 to¦23452 Far'oh¦23452 and¦23453 told¦23453 \add him\add*, “My¦23454 father¦23454 and¦23455 brothers¦23455 and¦23456 their¦23456 flocks¦23456 and¦23457 herds¦23457 and¦23458 everything that¦23460 \add belongs\add* to¦23461 them¦23461, have¦23462 come¦23462 from¦23463 Canaan¦23464 and¦23465 they're¦23465 \add here now\add* Goshen¦23467 \add area\add*.”
\v 2 Then¦23469 he¦23471 took¦23471 five¦23472 of his¦23470 brothers¦23470 and¦23474 presented¦23474 them¦23474 to¦23475 Far'oh¦23476,
\v 3 and¦23478 Far'oh¦23479 \add asked them\add*, “What's¦23483 your occupation¦23485?”
\p “Your¦23485 servants¦23492 have been shepherds \add for several generations\add*,” they¦23486 \add ≈replied¦23486\add*.
\v 4 Then¦23500 they¦23500 \add explained\add*, “We've¦23506 come¦23506 to \add stay here for a while\add* because¦23507 in¦23518 Canaan¦23519, there's¦23509 no pasture¦23510 for¦23511 our flocks¦23511 because¦23514 \add the drought is very severe\add*. So¦23520 now¦23520, please¦23523 let¦23521 your¦23524 servants¦23524 settle¦23521 in¦23525 the Goshen¦23526 \add area\add*.”
\v 5 Then¦23528 Far'oh¦23529 turned to¦23530 Yosef¦23532, “Your¦23534 father¦23534 and¦23535 your¦23535 brothers¦23535 have¦23536 come¦23536 to¦23537 you¦23537.
\v 6 The¦23539 \add entire country\add* of¦23539 Egypt¦23540 is in front¦23541 of you. Settle¦23545 your¦23548 father¦23548 and¦23549 your¦23551 brothers¦23551 in the¦23543 best¦23543 land¦23544, \add so\add* let¦23552 them¦23552 settle¦23552 in¦23553 the Goshen¦23554 \add area\add*. And¦23555 if¦23555 you're¦23557 \add aware\add* that¦23569 \add some of them have special talents\add*, then appoint¦23564 them¦23564 as overseers¦23565 of¦23565 \add my own\add* livestock¦23566 \add as well\add*.”
\p
\v 7 Then¦23573 Yosef¦23574 brought¦23573 his¦23578 father¦23578 Yacob and¦23579 presented him¦23579 to¦23580 Far'oh¦23581, and¦23582 Yacob¦23583 blessed¦23582 Far'oh¦23586.
\v 8 “How¦23593 \add old are you\add*?” Far'oh¦23589 asked¦23588 \add *him¦23592\add*.
