\v 11 \add ≈So¦23635\add* Yosef¦23636 gave¦23643 his¦23639 father¦23639 and¦23640 his¦23642 brothers¦23642 \add some of the best land\add* in¦23646 Egypt¦23647 and \add helped\add* them settle¦23635 there—in¦23648 the Rameses¦23651 \add district just\add* as¦23652 Far'oh¦23654 had¦23653 commanded¦23653.
\v 12 \add He also\add* provided¦23656 his¦23660 father¦23660 and¦23661 his¦23663 brothers¦23663 and¦23664 all¦23665 his¦23668 father's¦23668 household¦23667 with bread¦23669—each family according to¦23670 the \add number of children\add*.
\s1 Yosef's leadership through extreme famine
\rem /s1 Joseph's Leadership in the Famine; Joseph and the Famine; The Famine; The Famine in Egypt
\p
\v 13 \add Then the time came when\add* there¦23674 was¦23674 no bread¦23673 in¦23675 \add that entire part of\add* the¦23677 world¦23677, because¦23678 the \add drought\add* was \add now\add* extremely severe, and¦23683 \add both\add* Egypt¦23685 and¦23686 Canaan¦23687 were \add suffering from food shortages\add*.
\v 14 \add People all over came\add* to buy¦23708 grain, and¦23691 \add over time\add* Yosef¦23692 had received \add in payment\add* all¦23695 the¦23697 silver that¦23698 could be¦23698 found¦23698 in¦23699 Egypt¦23701 and¦23702 Canaan¦23703, and¦23709 \add *he¦23710\add* \add in turn\add* took¦23709 it¦23709 to¦23714 Far'oh's¦23715 house¦23714.
\v 15 \add ≈So¦23717\add* \add once there was no more silver left\add* in Egypt¦23720 and¦23721 in Canaan¦23722, all¦23724 \add the Egyptians\add* demanded from Yosef¦23729, “Give us food¦23734. Why should we¦23736 die¦23736 \add ≈right here in¦23737 front¦23737 of¦23737\add* you¦23737? \add All our money\add* is gone!”
\p
\v 16 “Bring your livestock,” Yosef¦23743 \add ≈answered¦23742\add*, “and I'll¦23746 give¦23746 grain to¦23747 you¦23747 in exchange for¦23748 \add them\add*, since the silver is gone.”
\v 17 \add ≈So¦23754\add* \add the people\add* brought¦23754 their livestock to¦23758 \add *him¦23760\add*, and¦23761 \add *he\add* gave¦23761 them¦23762 grain \add in exchange for\add* \add &their\add* horses¦23765 and¦23766 sheep¦23767 and¦23768 cattle and¦23770 donkeys¦23770. So¦23771 he¦23771 provided¦23771 them¦23771 with¦23772 food¦23772 that¦23777 year¦23776 \add in exchange\add* for all¦23773 their livestock.
\p
\v 18 \add The next\add* year¦23780 they¦23782 came¦23782 to¦23783 \add @Yosef¦23783\add* and¦23786 \add begged\add*, “We¦23790 can't hide¦23790 it from¦23791 our master¦23791 that¦23792 since \add there's no silver left\add* and¦23797 \add since all\add* the livestock \add now\add* belongs to¦23799 our lord, there's nothing left¦23803 \add to offer other than\add* our¦23809 \add #bodies¦23809\add* and¦23810 our¦23810 \add #lands¦23810\add*.
\v 19 Why should we¦23813 die¦23813 \add right in front of you\add*—both¦23815 we¦23817 and our land? Buy¦23820 us¦23822 and¦23823 our land in exchange for¦23826 food¦23826, and¦23827 we and our land will be slaves¦23830 to Far'oh¦23831. And¦23832 give¦23832 us seed¦23834 so¦23835 that¦23835 we'll¦23835 live¦23835 and¦23836 not¦23836 die¦23837, and¦23838 so that the¦23838 land¦23838 won't¦23839 be¦23840 barren.”
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦23842\add* Yosef¦23843 bought¦23842 all¦23846 the¦23848 farmland of¦23848 Egypt¦23849 for¦23850 Far'oh¦23850, because¦23851 every Egyptian¦23854 sold¦23853 his¦23856 field¦23856. \add In that way, all\add* the land became¦23862 Far'oh's¦23864 because the¦23861 famine¦23861 was \add so extreme\add*.
\v 21 \add As for\add* the¦23868 people¦23868, he¦23869 moved them to¦23871 the cities¦23871\f + \fr 47:21 \ft TC: There's a variation here in different early copies and translations. Rather than moving the people into the cities (which might have been done to make food distribution more efficient), some translations choose the alternative ‘made the people slaves’.\f* from¦23872 one end¦23872 of¦23872 Egypt¦23875 to¦23876 the other.
\v 22 The only¦23880 land¦23881 he¦23884 didn't buy¦23884 was that¦23894 of¦23881 the¦23882 priests¦23882, because¦23885 they \add were given a regular allowance\add* by Far'oh. Because they \add could live on what they were supplied with\add*, they didn't \add need to\add* sell¦23902 their land.
\v 23 Then¦23907 Yosef¦23908 told¦23907 the¦23911 people¦23911, “Listen, now that I've¦23913 bought¦23913 you¦23914 and¦23916 your¦23918 land¦23918 for¦23919 Far'oh¦23919, here¦23920 is¦23923 seed¦23923 for you so¦23924 that you¦23924 can \add work\add* the¦23927 ground¦23927.
\v 24 \add Every time\add* you harvest¦23930 \add a crop\add*, you¦23931 must¦23931 give¦23931 a¦23932 fifth¦23932 \add of it\add* to¦23933 Far'oh¦23933. The \add other\add* four¦23934 parts will¦23936 be for¦23937 you¦23937 \add to use\add* as seed¦23938 and¦23940 as food¦23940 for yourselves and your¦23942 households¦23942 and¦23943 your¦23944 young¦23944 children.”
\p
\v 25 “You've¦23947 kept¦23947 us¦23947 alive¦23947,” they \add agreed\add*. “Master¦23952, \add continue to show us your favour\add*, and¦23953 we'll¦23953 be¦23953 slaves¦23954 for Far'oh¦23955.”
\v 26 \add ≈So¦23957\add* Yosef¦23959 established¦23957 it¦23958 as a¦23960 law to this¦23964 day¦23963 concerning the Egyptian¦23968 farmland: that¦23964 the¦23967 fifth belongs¦23969 to¦23969 Far'oh¦23969. (Only¦23971 the priests¦23973' land didn't¦23975 become Far'oh's¦23977.)
\s1 Yacob's burial request
\rem /s1 Jacob's Last Request; The Last Days of Jacob
\p
\v 27 \add ≈So¦23979\add* Yisra'el¦23980 \add !(Yacob¦23980) and his descendants\add* settled in¦23981 the Goshen¦23984 region¦23981 of¦23982 Egypt¦23982 and \add prospered\add*. The \add had many children\add* and \add quickly increased in number\add*.
\v 28 Yacob¦23992 resided \add *there¦23994\add* for seventeen years¦23997, and¦23998 \add by then\add* he¦23998 was¦23998 147 years old
\v 29 and¦24010 he was getting close¦24010 to¦24015 death¦24015, so¦24016 he¦24016 called¦24016 for his¦24018 son¦24018 Yosef¦24019 and¦24020 asked¦24020 him¦24021, “If¦24022, please¦24024, I¦24025 have¦24025 found¦24025 favour¦24026 in¦24027 your¦24027 eyes¦24027, please¦24030 \add give me your hand and promise to\add* deal with¦24035 me¦24035 in kindness¦24036 and¦24037 faithfulness¦24037. Please¦24040 don't¦24038 bury¦24041 me¦24041 in¦24042 Egypt¦24042.\x + \xo 47:29-30: \xt Gen 49:29-32; 50:6.\x*
\v 30 When¦24044 I \add ≈die\add*, I want to be buried with¦24045 my¦24047 ancestors¦24047, so¦24048 carry¦24048 me¦24048 out of Egypt¦24049 and¦24050 bury¦24050 me¦24050 in¦24051 their¦24051 tomb¦24051.”
\p “I'll¦24054 do¦24054 \add what you've requested\add*,” \add @Yosef¦24055\add* \add agreed\add*.
\p
\v 31 “Promise¦24058 me¦24059,” he \add insisted\add*. So¦24060 \add @Yosef¦24060\add* \add promised\add* him¦24061 and¦24062 Yisra'el¦24063 bowed¦24062 at¦24064 the¦24066 head¦24066 of¦24066 the¦24067 bed¦24067.\f + \fr 47:31 \ft Some translations assume that elderly Yacob/Yisra'el bowed to God in worship after speaking with Yosef, but it's not impossible that he bowed to Yosef in acknowledgement of the high position that God had brought Yosef to as foretold by his dreams.\f*
\c 48
\s1 Yacob blesses Efrayim and Menashsheh
\rem /s1 Jacob Blesses Manasseh and Ephraim; Jacob Blesses Joseph's Sons; Jacob Blesses Ephraim and Manasseh; Manasseh and Ephraim
\p
\v 1 Some time after¦24071 that, Yosef¦24075 was told¦24074, “Listen, your¦24077 father¦24077 is¦24078 sick¦24078.” So¦24079 \add @Yosef¦24079\add* \add went to him\add*, taking¦24079 his two¦24082 sons¦24083 with¦24084 him¦24084—Manasseh¦24087 and¦24088 Efrayim¦24090.
\v 2 When¦24092 someone¦24092 told¦24092 Yacob¦24093 that Yosef¦24097 had¦24098 arrived¦24098, \add he\add* exerted himself¦24100 and¦24102 sat¦24102 up in bed¦24105,
\v 3 then¦24107 \add *he¦24108\add* told¦24107 \add *him¦24111\add*, “God¦24112 the provider appeared¦24114 to¦24116 me¦24116 at¦24117 Luz¦24117 in¦24118 Canaan¦24119, and¦24120 he¦24120 blessed¦24120 me¦24121\x + \xo 48:3-4: \xt Gen 28:13-14.\x*
\v 4 and¦24123 said¦24123 to¦24124 me¦24124, ‘Listen, I'll¦24125 make¦24126 you¦24126 fruitful¦24126, and¦24127 I'll¦24127 multiply¦24127 you¦24127 and¦24128 make¦24128 you¦24128 into¦24129 a¦24129 community of¦24129 peoples¦24130. And¦24131 I'll¦24131 give¦24131 this¦24135 land¦24134 to¦24136 your¦24136 offspring¦24136 after¦24137 you¦24137 to be their possession¦24138 forever¦24139.’
\v 5 “And¦24141 now¦24141, your two¦24142 sons¦24144, who¦24145 were¦24145 born¦24145 for¦24146 you \add here\add* in¦24147 Egypt¦24148 before I came¦24151 \add here\add*, I¦24151 \add adopt\add* them as my own—Efrayim¦24157 and¦24158 Manasseh¦24158—just as¦24159 Reuben¦24159 and¦24160 Simeon¦24160 are mine.
\v 6 \add Any other\add* children¦24165 that you¦24168 father¦24168 after¦24169 them¦24169 will be¦24175 yours. Their¦24176 inheritance¦24176 will \add only be through their older\add* brothers¦24174.
\v 7 As for me, \add when\add* I¦24178 was coming¦24180 into¦24185 Canaan¦24186 from¦24181 Paddan¦24181, Rahel¦24184 died¦24182 beside on¦24187 the way¦24187 when¦24180 we were still quite some distance¦24189 from Efrath, and¦24194 I¦24194 buried¦24194 her¦24194 there¦24195 beside the¦24196 road of¦24196 Efrath¦24197 (which¦24198 is¦24199 Bethlehem).”\x + \xo 48:7: \xt Gen 35:16-19.\x*
\p
\v 8 Then¦24202 Yisra'el¦24203 \add noticed\add* Yosef's¦24207 \add two\add* sons¦24206 and¦24208 \add asked\add*, “Who¦24209 are¦24211 these¦24211?”
\p
\v 9 “They are¦24218 my¦24218 sons¦24218 that¦24232 God¦24225 has¦24222 given¦24222 me¦24224 \add here\add* in¦24226 this¦24226 place¦24226.” Yosef¦24214 \add ≈replied¦24227\add* to his¦24217 father¦24217.
\p “Please¦24230 bring¦24228 them¦24228 to¦24231 me¦24231, and I¦24232 will bless¦24232 them¦24232,” \add @Yacob\add* \add requested\add*.
\v 10 Now Yisra'el's¦24235 sight¦24234 was¦24236 poor in \add &his\add* old¦24237 age¦24237, so he¦24239 wasn't able¦24239 to¦24240 see¦24240 \add much\add*. So¦24241 \add @Yosef¦24241\add* brought¦24241 them¦24242 over to¦24243 him¦24243, and¦24244 \add @Yisra'el¦24244\add* kissed¦24244 them¦24245 and¦24246 embraced¦24246 them¦24247.
\v 11 “I \add never expected to see you again\add*” \add he\add* said¦24249 to¦24251 Yosef¦24253, “but¦24258 wow¦24258, God¦24261 has¦24259 \add even\add* let me¦24260 see your¦24265 children¦24265 as well.”
\v 12 Then¦24267 Yosef¦24268 removed¦24267 \add his sons\add* from¦24270 his \add father's\add* knees¦24271 and¦24272 bowed¦24272 with his¦24273 face¦24273 to the¦24274 ground¦24274.
\p
\v 13 Then¦24276 Yosef¦24277 took¦24276 both¦24280 of¦24280 them¦24280—Efrayim¦24283 on his¦24284 right¦24284 toward Yisra'el's¦24286 left and¦24287 Manasseh¦24289 \add (the eldest)\add* on his¦24290 left¦24290 toward Yisra'el's¦24292 right—and¦24293 brought¦24293 them¦24293 close¦24293 to¦24294 him¦24294.
\v 14 But¦24296 Yisra'el¦24297 intentionally extended¦24296 his¦24300 right¦24300 hand and¦24301 placed¦24301 it on¦24302 the¦24304 Efrayim's¦24305 head (the¦24307 younger¦24307 one), and¦24308 \add crossing his arms,\add* he placed his¦24310 left¦24310 hand on¦24311 Manasseh's head.
\v 15 Then¦24323 he¦24323 blessed¦24323 Yosef¦24326 saying¦24327,
\q1 “May the¦24328 god who¦24329 my¦24331 \add grandfather\add* Abraham¦24333 and¦24334 my father¦24331 Yitshak¦24334 \add served\add*,
\q1 the¦24335 god who¦24336 has been shepherding¦24336 me¦24337 \add for my entire life\add*,
\q1
\v 16 the¦24344 messenger¦24344 who's¦24345 \add turned all harm intended for me into good\add*,
\q2 may¦24350 he¦24350 bless¦24350 these young men.
\q1 May¦24354 they be¦24354 recognised \add as my descendants\add*,
\q2 and¦24357 as \add descendants\add* of Abraham¦24359 and¦24360 Yitshak¦24360,
\q1 and¦24361 grow to¦24362 increase¦24362 in¦24362 number¦24362 on the¦24364 earth¦24364.
\p
\v 17 Then¦24366 Yosef¦24367 noticed¦24366 that¦24368 his¦24371 father¦24371 had placed¦24370 his¦24374 right¦24374 hand on¦24375 Efrayim's¦24378 head and¦24379 he was¦24379 upset about¦24380 it, so¦24381 he¦24381 picked up his¦24384 father's¦24384 hand to¦24385 move it¦24386 across to Manasseh's¦24394 head,
\v 18 telling¦24396 his¦24400 father¦24400, “My¦24404 father¦24404, that's wrong because¦24405 that¦24407 one is¦24408 my oldest¦24408 son. Put¦24409 your¦24410 right¦24410 hand¦24410 on¦24411 \em his¦24413\em* head¦24413.”
\v 19 But his¦24416 father¦24416 \add pushed back\add*, “I¦24418 know¦24418, my¦24419 son¦24419, I¦24420 know¦24420. \add @Manasseh\add* will¦24424 also become¦24424 a¦24426 people¦24426, and¦24427 he will¦24430 also be great¦24430. Nevertheless his¦24432 younger brother¦24432 will be the greater¦24434 one, and¦24436 his¦24436 descendants will¦24437 become a multitude of¦24438 nations¦24440.”
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦24442\add* \add @Yisra'el¦24442\add* blessed¦24442 \add @Efrayim¦24442 and¦24442 Manasseh¦24442\add* that day¦24443 saying¦24445,\x + \xo 48:20: \xt Heb 11:21.\x*
